%% Blockchain Flow — Diagram 8. Source: Blockchain-integration.md §11.
%% IMPLEMENTED: everything below. DEMO/SIMULATION: single-node ordering only —
%% the cryptography (signing, hashing, Merkle proofs) is real.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Svc as Service layer
    participant Client as Ledger client
    participant CC as Chaincode contract
    participant Ord as Orderer (single-node, DEMO)
    participant WS as World state

    Svc->>Client: submit(contract, function, args, submitter_msp)
    Client->>CC: simulate against current world state
    CC-->>Client: read_set, write_set (or ContractError — no block produced)
    Client->>Client: collect endorsements per policy (ECDSA P-256)
    Client->>Client: submitter signs the transaction
    Client->>Ord: signed transaction
    Ord->>Ord: verify all signatures, cut block\n(SHA-256 hash-linked, Merkle root)
    Ord->>WS: commit write_set
    Ord-->>Svc: tx_id, block_number, content_hash
    Note over Svc,WS: Verification later: GET /blockchain/verify\nreplays every block and re-checks every signature
